class.description:
A tree owns one [NetwMultiplayer] and installs it on its own branch of the [SceneTree], so every descendant answers [method Netw.of] with that session and two trees in one [SceneTree] are two independent sessions. It carries the exports that configure the session and nothing else: the state, the role, the roster and the service registry all belong to [member api]. A session comes online the ordinary Godot way, by assigning a [MultiplayerPeer]. The tree publishes no verb for that, because the assignment IS the bring-up. An assignment made while a declaration is still being authored is refused rather than silently deferred, so bring up through [method Netw.connection] or wait for the deferred settle. [member app_id], [member desired_role] and [member link_conditions] are the session's whole FALLBACK, used when no node declared one through [method Netw.configure_session]. An explicit declaration replaces them whole: no field is merged, and any non-default export it discards is named once in a warning. Once the session has consumed its configuration these exports are immutable, and a setter reports the late write and keeps its old value. [codeblock] tree.peer_class = &"ENetMultiplayerPeer" tree.transport_settings = { port = 21253 }
# A peer the game already holds. var peer := ENetMultiplayerPeer.new() peer.create_client("127.0.0.1", 21253) tree.api.session_prepare_join(&"PlayerOne", []) tree.api.multiplayer_peer = peer
# Or one the provider knows how to build, prepared and assigned inside # the window the offer arrives in. Netw.connection(tree).create_peer( tree.peer_class, NetwMultiplayer.TRANSPORT_MODE_CLIENT, "127.0.0.1:21253", tree.transport_settings, func(peer: MultiplayerPeer, error: Error, _detail: String) -> void: if error == OK: tree.api.session_prepare_join(&"PlayerOne", []) tree.api.multiplayer_peer = peer, ) [/codeblock] The tree brings itself up in exactly two cases, both of which have no caller to answer to: a headless build with [member auto_host_headless] set, and a debug build carrying a [member debug_join]. Everything else is the game's own composition.
